From: CodeAndSolder <codeandsolder@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] json_object: return zero directly on invalid integer strings

Both integer getters already return zero when parsing a string fails:
the string switch case falls through to default solely to return 0.
A bare FALLTHRU comment is not accepted under the target's strict
-Wimplicit-fallthrough setting.

Make that behavior explicit and return 0 directly. This does not
change valid or invalid conversion semantics.

---
--- a/json_object.c
+++ b/json_object.c
@@ -1018,7 +1018,7 @@
 	case json_type_string:
 		if (json_parse_int64(get_string_component(jso), &cint) == 0)
 			return cint;
-		/* FALLTHRU */
+		return 0;
 	default: return 0;
 	}
 }
@@ -1071,7 +1071,7 @@
 	case json_type_string:
 		if (json_parse_uint64(get_string_component(jso), &cuint) == 0)
 			return cuint;
-		/* FALLTHRU */
+		return 0;
 	default: return 0;
 	}
 }
